Keeps skshaper from calling SkUnicodes::Libgrapheme::Make.

With skia_use_libgrapheme the get_unicode() helpers in SkShaper_harfbuzz.cpp
and SkShaper_skunicode.cpp try libgrapheme after ICU. The legacy factories
(SkShaper::Make, MakeShaperDrivenWrapper, ...) call them, so skshaper.lib
needed skunicode_libgrapheme.lib in every text consumer, also in one that
never wants the fallback.

This drops that branch. The helpers try ICU only, as they did without
libgrapheme. SkShapers::BestAvailableUnicode() in utils/FactoryHelpers.h is
header-only and compiled with the consumer's defines, so a consumer that
defines SK_UNICODE_LIBGRAPHEME_IMPLEMENTATION and links the fallback archive
still gets ICU first and libgrapheme second from it.

diff --git a/modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_harfbuzz.cpp b/modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_harfbuzz.cpp
index abeb937..dd3096f 100644
--- a/modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_harfbuzz.cpp
+++ b/modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_harfbuzz.cpp
@@ -1592,11 +1592,9 @@ static sk_sp<SkUnicode> get_unicode() {
         return unicode;
     }
 #endif  // defined(SK_UNICODE_ICU_IMPLEMENTATION)
-#if defined(SK_UNICODE_LIBGRAPHEME_IMPLEMENTATION)
-    if (auto unicode = SkUnicodes::Libgrapheme::Make()) {
-        return unicode;
-    }
-#endif
+    // skia-prep: libgrapheme is not tried here (skia-157-separable-libgrapheme.patch).
+    // A consumer that links skunicode_libgrapheme gets it through
+    // SkShapers::BestAvailableUnicode().
 #if defined(SK_UNICODE_ICU4X_IMPLEMENTATION)
     if (auto unicode = SkUnicodes::ICU4X::Make()) {
         return unicode;
